      "content": "Rubbing vigorously can cause more harm than good, and you don't want to scratch your eye. Apple cider vinegar is acidic, not alkaline, so it won't neutralize the cleaner. Instead, rinse your eye with cool water for 15-20 minutes. If the irritation persists, you can use a saline solution or a mixture of 1 part vinegar to 3 parts water, but only for a short period. If the pain or irritation doesn't subside, seek medical help immediately. Remember, your eye is precious, and it's better to be safe than sorry.",
